{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Root Cause Requirement",
  "description": "When the user reports a bug, error, failure, or broken behavior, forces the agent to obtain evidence before proposing a fix.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "promptSubmit"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "BUG REPORT CHECK. Inspect the user's most recent message. If it clearly reports a defect, failure, error, broken behavior, regression, crash, incorrect output, or something that does not work, do not propose a fix immediately. First obtain evidence. Use the most appropriate available method for this project: inspect existing scripts, run an existing validation command, run a relevant test, reproduce manually with a small command, inspect logs, or read the failing code path. Do not invent commands. If no executable validation path exists yet, state that clearly and use static evidence from the codebase instead. Only after evidence is captured may you state a hypothesis or propose a change. If the message does not report a defect, ignore this hook and proceed normally."
  }
}